sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as 🐍 Python SDK
    participant API as 🚪 REST API
    participant Handlers as 🔄 Unified Handlers
    participant CS as 📁 CollectionService
    participant Engine as 💾 Storage Engine
    participant TxCoord as 🔄 Transaction Coordinator
    participant Storage as ☁️ Cloud Storage

    Note over Client,Storage: 📋 Collection Management with Storage Assignment

    %% Collection Creation Flow
    Client->>+API: POST /collections<br/>CollectionConfig + compression settings
    API->>+Handlers: handle_collection_operation()<br/>JSON → Proto conversion & validation
    Handlers->>+CS: create_collection()<br/>Metadata setup with storage assignment
    
    CS->>CS: Generate unique collection ID<br/>Assign storage locations
    Note over CS: Creates StorageAssignment:<br/>• data_location: /data/collections/{id}<br/>• wal_location: /wal/collections/{id}<br/>• compression_config: SDK-provided
    
    CS->>+Engine: initialize_storage()<br/>Setup storage with assignment
    Engine->>+TxCoord: setup_collection_storage()<br/>Atomic directory creation
    TxCoord->>+Storage: create_collection_dirs()<br/>Create at specified paths
    Storage-->>-TxCoord: Directories created successfully
    TxCoord-->>-Engine: Storage paths ready
    Engine-->>-CS: Collection storage initialized
    
    CS->>CS: Persist collection metadata<br/>Include storage_assignment in proto
    CS-->>-Handlers: Collection created with assignment
    Handlers-->>-API: Proto → JSON response
    API-->>-Client: Collection details + storage info

    %% Collection Retrieval Flow
    Note over Client,Storage: 📖 Collection Metadata Retrieval

    Client->>+API: GET /collections/{id}
    API->>+Handlers: handle_get_collection()
    Handlers->>+CS: get_collection(id)
    CS->>CS: Load from metadata store<br/>Include storage_assignment
    CS-->>-Handlers: Collection with storage info
    Handlers-->>-API: Proto → JSON conversion
    API-->>-Client: Collection metadata + storage assignment

    %% Collection Listing Flow
    Note over Client,Storage: 📚 Collection Listing

    Client->>+API: GET /collections
    API->>+Handlers: handle_list_collections()
    Handlers->>+CS: list_collections()
    CS->>CS: Query metadata store<br/>Filter by permissions
    CS-->>-Handlers: List of collections
    Handlers-->>-API: Proto → JSON array
    API-->>-Client: Collection list with metadata

    %% Collection Update Flow
    Note over Client,Storage: ✏️ Collection Configuration Update

    Client->>+API: PUT /collections/{id}/config<br/>Updated compression settings
    API->>+Handlers: handle_update_collection()
    Handlers->>+CS: update_collection_config()
    CS->>CS: Validate configuration changes<br/>Update storage_assignment if needed
    CS->>CS: Persist updated metadata<br/>Atomic update operation
    CS-->>-Handlers: Configuration updated
    Handlers-->>-API: Success response
    API-->>-Client: Updated collection config

    %% Collection Deletion Flow
    Note over Client,Storage: 🗑️ Collection Deletion with Cleanup

    Client->>+API: DELETE /collections/{id}
    API->>+Handlers: handle_delete_collection()
    Handlers->>+CS: delete_collection(id)
    
    CS->>+Engine: cleanup_collection_storage(id)<br/>Remove all data files
    Engine->>+TxCoord: begin_cleanup_operation()<br/>Atomic cleanup transaction
    TxCoord->>+Storage: delete_collection_dirs()<br/>Remove directories & files
    Storage-->>-TxCoord: Cleanup completed
    TxCoord-->>-Engine: Storage cleanup confirmed
    Engine-->>-CS: Collection storage removed
    
    CS->>CS: Remove from metadata store<br/>Final cleanup step
    CS-->>-Handlers: Collection deleted successfully
    Handlers-->>-API: Deletion confirmed
    API-->>-Client: Success response

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over CS: **📁 Storage Assignment Benefits**<br/>• Automatic path generation<br/>• Multi-disk support<br/>• Cloud storage integration<br/>• ACID transaction guarantees
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 220)
        Note over TxCoord: **🔄 Transaction Coordinator**<br/>• Atomic operations<br/>• Rollback on failure<br/>• Multi-backend consistency<br/>• Staging-based operations
    end